From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:41:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(hub): make all 6 cards a uniform size

The cards grid (auto-rows-fr) sits inside a naturally-growing scroll
container with no fixed height, so auto-rows-fr has no definite height
to distribute and silently behaves like auto-rows-max: each row ends
up sized independently by its own content. A row whose subtitle text
is longer (e.g. 'Kadhi Pakora', 'Kurukshetra') renders visibly taller
than a row with a short one ('Chandigarh'), so different states (and
even different rows within the same state) showed differently-sized
cards instead of a uniform grid.

Added min-h-[10rem] to HubCard so every card shares the same height
floor regardless of its row's content - comfortably fits the worst
case (icon/badge row + a full 2-line clamped subtitle + the bottom
count/arrow row) so all 6 cards now render the same size.
